PS5 VRR on FLAVA3 consoles, switched with Steam's VRR setting

Lawson's fix (his PS5 VRR kernel vrr13), on the GPU side; hsgodd's stock-system
captures had narrowed the problem down:
 - Sony's GPU sends the HDMI chip a timing packet every frame, a DP extension SDP
   (HB 39 04) with the source timing, from the adaptive-sync slot; on the chip it
   replaces amdgpu's FreeSync SDP, whatever the sync polarity
 - the chip drops its input lock when DPCD 0x107's MSA-ignore bit is set: the bit stays
   clear on the chip's link while the GPU varies the frame length (DRR)
 - the chip is switched to follow mode only after the packet flows (0x6064=03,
   0x1047=30, 0x600c=01 00, 0x6224=40 0f, 0x6c07=80, 250 ms apart), plus a FreeSync SPD
   in its SPD slot 0x7240; the picture stays muted until it has switched over
VRR is offered when the TV's EDID has a VRR range (HDMI Forum VSDB, else the FreeSync
VSDB), on the HDMI chip's connector only (never the USB-C port), and Steam's VRR
setting switches it; switching re-runs the chip setup once. Tested at 4K60, 1080p120,
1440p60 and 1440p120 on an LG C4 (Gilles).
 - VRR only on FLAVA3: on VERDE consoles (and with hdmi.vrr=0) it is never offered on the
   HDMI chip, whatever the generic DP path concludes
 - hdmi.vrr=0: never offer VRR
 - hdmi.icc_trace=1: every message to the chip and its reply in the log (debugging)
 - hdmi.vrr_measure=1: the measured frame intervals every 2 s while VRR is on (debugging)
Replaces the v1.5.1-v1.6.3 VRR test patches.
